      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "A franchise that keeps insisting it can patch the roof while the weather is changing has turned its summer into a test of nerve. <strong>Mitch Marner's agent saying he was \"never protected\" by the Maple Leafs</strong> is the kind of public jab that lingers, because it speaks to the larger job now: building a harder, safer roster around the stars. Toronto finished 8th in the Atlantic with 78 points, and that finality has pushed the conversation where it belongs - on cap space, fit, and the draft class rather than nostalgia. Tyler Hopkins' invite to Hockey Canada's World Junior Summer Showcase is a useful reminder that the pipeline still matters. <strong>What happens next - with unsigned picks, free-agent trimming, and whether the Leafs add more bite down the middle - will tell you if this summer is repair work or just another repaint.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated July 25, 2026"
      },
