      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "The slide has become the story, and the alarm bell got louder Thursday night in Boston. <strong>Toronto fell 6-4 to the Red Sox</strong>, its third loss in four games since snapping a four-game skid with that 3-1 win over Tampa Bay, and the Blue Jays are now 47-57, fifth in the AL East, 13.5 games back. That is not a contender's footing; it is the edge of the deadline trapdoor. The offense has shown flashes, but the club keeps bleeding late - and when the margin is this thin, every missed inning feels bigger. The one bright spot was the brief lift from the Rays series win, but it vanished fast. <strong>They go back to Boston tonight at 4:10 PM ET, and Toronto needs a clean start before the market starts sorting buyers from sellers.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated July 25, 2026"
      },
