      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Raptors",
        "body": "The offseason has turned into a roster sorting exercise, and Toronto is right in the middle of it. <strong>Allen Graves' emergence at Summer League has made the first-round pick look like more than a draft-night headline</strong>, a useful sign for a team trying to stack real length and defense around its core. Toronto finished 3rd in the Atlantic Division, but that old number matters only as a frame for the work ahead; this is now about trimming the edges and getting the two-way spots right. Seth Lundy has been floated as the best fit for the final two-way contract, while Sharp's move to the Clippers only sharpens the competition. Add the Kawhi uncertainty hovering over the trade return, and the front office has a delicate hand on the wheel. <strong>Watch the two-way market and the Kawhi resolution - both could reshape the depth chart fast.</strong>",
